        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx1.256$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}5^{2x}&=\\log_{10}6^{x+1}\\\\2x\\log_{10}5&=(x+1)\\log_{10}6\\\\2x\\log_{10}5&=x\\log_{10}6+\\log_{10}6\\\\2x\\log_{10}5-x\\log_{10}6&=\\log_{10}6\\\\x(2\\log_{10}5-\\log_{10}6)&=\\log_{10}6\\\\x&=\\frac{\\log_{10}6}{2\\log_{10}5-\\log_{10}6}\\\\x&\\approx1.256\\end{align*}$$\nTo 4 s.f.",
